	abstract = {Several studies have demonstrated how Dynamic Line Rating ({DLR}) could be an effective solution for increasing transmission capacity of existing overhead lines. As opposed to Static Line Ratings ({SLR}), {DLR} allows for higher power flows depending on real time thermal state of conductors, which highly depend on actual weather conditions. Similarly, recent advances in transformer thermal modelling revealed the feasibility of Dynamic Transformer Rating ({DTR}) based on the temporal evolution of top oil and winding hot spot temperatures. However, the joint dynamic thermal rating of both overhead lines and transformers in transmission networks has not been thoroughly addressed yet in the literature.},
